// Consensus reference vectors for the heavyhash self-test (see heavyhash.c).
// Machine-generated; DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
//
// Group 1, whole-hash over an 80-byte header: covers the seed derivation,
// matrix generation, both SHA3 passes, nibble packing and the digest byte order.
// [0] and [1] are the OBTC main and test net genesis headers; obtc-core
// src/chainparams.cpp asserts each resulting hash, and CBlockHeader::GetHash()
// is GetPoWHash(), so the asserted block id is the heavyhash digest. Expected
// bytes are the internal little-endian order, i.e. the reverse of the displayed
// hash. [2] carries a non-zero prevhash, which neither genesis header has, so it
// is the only vector that would catch the matrix seed reading the wrong 32 bytes.
//
// Group 2, core only: obtc-core's own vectors from test/functional/heavy_hash.py
// against its hardcoded reference matrix. These pin the matrix multiply, the
// >> 10 reduction, the nibble order and the xor independently of matrix
// generation, so a compensating pair of errors cannot hide.

